.TH START-TMUX.SH 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
start-tmux.sh \- build the shifter tmux workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start-tmux.sh
[\fB\-s\fR \fIsession\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR \fIdirectory\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B start-tmux.sh
lays out a tmux session for general shift work. The first window,
\fBdaq\-main\fR, is split into four tiled panes; the second,
\fBbuild\fR, into two side by side.
.PP
.RS
.nf
|---------------------------|---------------------------|
| main                      | monitor                   |
|---------------------------|---------------------------|
| env A                     | env B                     |
|---------------------------|---------------------------|
.fi
.RE
.PP
This command only creates panes; it starts no DAQ processes. It is
independent of
.BR start-daq.sh (1),
which builds its own session, and both can be running at once.
.PP
If the session already exists it is left alone, and \fB\-a\fR attaches
to it.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-session " " \fINAME\fR
Session name. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_TMUX_SESSION\fR. Default:
\fIdaq\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-directory " " \fIDIR\fR
Starting directory for every pane. Environment:
\fBMU2EDAQ_TMUX_CWD\fR. Default: the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-attach
Attach once the layout is built.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the tmux commands and create nothing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Trace execution with \fBset \-x\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B START_TMUX_SH_OPTS
Extra options, prepended to the command line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success or when the session already existed, 1 if tmux is
missing or the starting directory does not exist, and 2 for an
unrecognised option.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build the workspace in the shifter's home directory and attach:
.PP
.RS
.nf
start-tmux.sh -d ~ -a
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-daq.sh (1),
.BR daq-status.sh (1),
.BR tmux (1)
